WEBVTT

1
00:00:13.787 --> 00:00:16.829
Jimmy left, Pollyanna and Aunt Polly sat down to lunch.

2
00:00:18.169 --> 00:00:23.012
Pollyanna tried to speak, but gave up when she almost said "glad" five times.

3
00:00:27.215 --> 00:00:29.236
Aunt Polly shook her head and sighed.

4
00:00:30.624 --> 00:00:33.446
"Just go ahead and say the word, Pollyanna."

5
00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:36.168
"Oh, thank you!"

6
00:00:37.069 --> 00:00:39.070
Pollyanna looked up from her soup and smiled.

7
00:00:39.090 --> 00:00:43.854
"It's pretty hard not to say it because I've played the game for so long."

8
00:00:43.874 --> 00:00:46.496
"You've what?"

9
00:00:46.516 --> 00:00:51.039
"Played the game that Father Pollyanna blushed.

10
00:00:52.140 --> 00:00:54.261
That was another word she wasn't supposed to say.

11
00:00:55.702 --> 00:00:57.844
Aunt Polly buttered a roll and said nothing.

12
00:00:59.692 --> 00:01:03.114
The rest of the meal was silent except for the clinking of silverware on china.

13
00:01:05.856 --> 00:01:10.619
After lunch Pollyanna was playing with Buffy, the dog, when she heard Aunt Polly on the telephone.

14
00:01:11.680 --> 00:01:16.463
Aunt Polly was telling someone that she'd be unable to attend the Ladies' Aid meeting because of a

15
00:01:16.523 --> 00:01:22.707
headache. Then she went upstairs to her room and closed the door.

16
00:01:22.727 --> 00:01:29.512
"I'm sorry Aunt Polly has a headache," Pollyanna said as she petted Buffy.

17
00:01:30.868 --> 00:01:33.490
"But I'm glad she won't be at the meeting this afternoon.

18
00:01:33.510 --> 00:01:38.535
I wouldn't want her calling Jimmy 'a little beggar' in front of everyone."

19
00:01:40.036 --> 00:01:44.420
Pollyanna knew that the Ladies' Aid meeting was scheduled for two o'clock in the church social hall.

20
00:01:45.761 --> 00:01:47.623
But she had already decided to arrive late.

21
00:01:47.643 --> 00:01:54.068
"I want all the ladies to be there before I start talking about Jimmy," she explained to Buffy.

22
00:01:54.088 --> 00:01:57.852
"The more people who hear about him, the better."

23
00:01:58.828 --> 00:02:00.709
Buffy wagged his tail in agreement.

24
00:02:04.012 --> 00:02:06.233
Pollyanna left home around half past two.

25
00:02:08.735 --> 00:02:13.318
With quiet confidence, she entered the social hall and stood for a moment, listening for voices.

26
00:02:17.861 --> 00:02:20.823
Following the sound, she entered a large room filled with ladies.

27
00:02:21.664 --> 00:02:23.205
The chatter immediately stopped.

28
00:02:24.226 --> 00:02:27.508
Everyone turned to look at Pollyanna, and she suddenly felt shy.

29
00:02:28.800 --> 00:02:33.604
These were not her own dear Ladies' Aiders from her church out West, but a group of strangers.

30
00:02:33.624 --> 00:02:38.388
"How do you do, Ladies' Aiders?"

31
00:02:38.808 --> 00:02:39.969
Pollyanna said bravely.

32
00:02:39.989 --> 00:02:43.152
"I'm Pollyanna Whittier.

33
00:02:43.592 --> 00:02:45.714
I guess some of you know me—maybe?"

34
00:02:47.355 --> 00:02:49.477
Pollyanna could feel the silence filling the room.

35
00:02:50.658 --> 00:02:53.981
Some of the ladies had met Pollyanna, and almost all of them had heard of her.

36
00:02:55.342 --> 00:02:57.504
But no one could think of anything to say to her.

37
00:02:58.812 --> 00:03:03.215
After a moment Pollyanna remembered what she'd heard her father say to the Ladies' Aiders back home.

38
00:03:05.216 --> 00:03:08.438
She coughed slightly before addressing them in a clear, loud voice.

39
00:03:08.458 --> 00:03:11.519
"I've come to lay a case before you."

40
00:03:13.220 --> 00:03:16.002
There was a slight rustle as the ladies sat up to pay attention.

41
00:03:16.022 --> 00:03:19.824
"Did your aunt send you, my dear?"

42
00:03:20.504 --> 00:03:22.626
Mrs. Ford, the minister's wife, asked.

43
00:03:23.886 --> 00:03:24.507
"Oh, no.

44
00:03:25.107 --> 00:03:26.468
I came all by myself.

45
00:03:28.992 --> 00:03:32.815
You see, I'm used to Ladies' Aiders because they helped Father bring me up."

46
00:03:34.677 --> 00:03:36.639
A few of the ladies raised their eyebrows.

47
00:03:36.659 --> 00:03:39.541
"But why are you here?"

48
00:03:40.061 --> 00:03:41.102
Mrs. Ford asked.

49
00:03:41.122 --> 00:03:48.889
"Jimmy Bean hasn't any home except the orphanage, and he doesn't think anyone there really wants him.

50
00:03:50.190 --> 00:03:52.632
He'd like a home with a family who'll care about him.

51
00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.896
He's almost 11, and I thought some of you might want him."

52
00:03:57.344 --> 00:03:59.705
Pollyanna paused, hoping someone would speak.

53
00:04:00.785 --> 00:04:02.665
"To live with you," she quickly added.

54
00:04:03.966 --> 00:04:06.326
A woman in a red hat finally broke the silence.

55
00:04:06.346 --> 00:04:09.107
"Did you ever hear anything like it?"

56
00:04:09.427 --> 00:04:10.688
she murmured to the others.

57
00:04:12.108 --> 00:04:15.329
With anxious eyes, Pollyanna examined the faces staring at her.

58
00:04:15.349 --> 00:04:19.230
"Oh, I almost forgot to say that he'll work!"

59
00:04:19.650 --> 00:04:20.410
she exclaimed.

60
00:04:22.871 --> 00:04:26.792
A few women questioned Pollyanna, and soon everyone understood what she was asking.

61
00:04:27.764 --> 00:04:29.925
Ignoring her, the women talked among themselves.

62
00:04:31.626 --> 00:04:35.869
No one wanted to take Jimmy, though some ladies thought others should because they had no sons.

63
00:04:35.889 --> 00:04:38.971
"Perhaps," Mrs.

64
00:04:39.051 --> 00:04:43.174
Ford said timidly, "there is something we can do as a group.

65
00:04:43.694 --> 00:04:49.618
We could assume responsibility for his care instead of supporting orphanages overseas."

66
00:04:50.978 --> 00:04:53.020
A great many women started talking at once.

67
00:04:54.560 --> 00:05:00.402
Pollyanna learned that this group of Ladies' Aiders was famous for donating large amounts of money to orphanages

68
00:05:00.562 --> 00:05:04.803
overseas. The woman in the red hat spoke again.

69
00:05:04.823 --> 00:05:09.124
"I would die of embarrassment if we contributed less this year."

70
00:05:10.605 --> 00:05:12.105
Another woman nodded in agreement.

71
00:05:12.125 --> 00:05:15.826
"We always top the list of big donors."

72
00:05:18.227 --> 00:05:21.188
Pollyanna said nothing and was soon glad to escape the meeting.

73
00:05:23.112 --> 00:05:28.821
"I don't understand why it's more important to top some list than to help Jimmy," she muttered.
